welcome to the class of 2022.  to start our online kickoff i thought  i'd take you outside  for a quick tour of some of my favorite  places at stamford  let's start at koopa you'll quickly  discover that there are several koopa  cafes on the stamford campus  the gsb one is the best it's the center  of activity on campus  and dean lowry's unofficial office  last week i was trying to keep a low  profile  but i had a chance meeting with a few  early arrivals from your class  that in my day  town square is the heart of the gsb  the tents and the outdoor furniture are  recent additions  phil knight's footsteps are a reminder  of the people who've come before you at  the gsb  and whose shoes you're filling when the  night management center was built  the artist peter wagner designed the  cornerstone  he perfectly captured the gsb  dedicated to the things that haven't  happened yet and the people  who are about to dream them up i first  came to stamford as an undergraduate  in 1990 and joined the faculty 10 years  later  i'm still amazed by the beauty of the  campus  the rodan sculpture garden is one of the  famous places on the stamford campus  and for those of you with children it's  one of the few museums that our kids  actually enjoy  some people think the koopa cafe near  green library is as good as the one at  the gsb  mistakenly i hope you all will make an  effort to experience stanford beyond the  gsb  and to meet the brilliant students and  faculty in law  medicine engineering education  sustainability and other fields  i promise it will inspire you  of course the physical campus is one  part of what makes stamford special  but it's not the important part it's the  people you will meet  and the relationships you'll form that  will truly make your time here memorable  so again welcome to the gsb we can't  wait to see what you dream up
 

